Passage: REG, Annex III, 1.2.6

[0] 1.2.6.
[1] Failure of the power supply or communication network connection The interruption, the re-establishment after an interruption or the fluctuation in whatever manner of the power supply or communication network connection to the machinery or related product shall not lead to hazardous situations.
[2] Particular attention shall be given to the following:
[3] (a) the machinery or related product shall not start unexpectedly;
[4] (b) the parameters of the machinery shall not change in an uncontrolled way when such change can lead to hazardous situations;
[5] (c) the machinery or related product shall not be prevented from stopping if the stop command has already been given;
[6] (d) no moving part of the machinery or related product or piece held by the machinery or related product shall fall or be ejected;
[7] (e) automatic or manual stopping of the moving parts, whatever they may be, shall be unimpeded;
[8] (f) the protective devices shall remain fully effective or give a stop command.
